  <ferc:DisclosureOfStatusOfAnyMateriallyImportantLegalProceedingsTextBlock id="f-25" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;9. See Note 11 Commitments and Contingent Liabilities on page 122-123. In addition, important proceedings related to the Cardinal Hickory Creek project occurring during this quarter is listed below:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;&#8226;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:36pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:8pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%;padding-left:15.2pt"&gt;On September 24, the U.S. District Court for the Western District of Wisconsin issued a final order in the federal land exchange litigation regarding the Cardinal Hickory Creek Transmission Line Project. In the ruling, Judge William Conley dismissed all claims against the federal defendants and co-owner utilities, and directed the clerk of the court to enter final judgment and close the case.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfStatusOfAnyMateriallyImportantLegalProceedingsTextBlock>
