    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-22" id="fn-22" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%">We have a net excess deferred income tax regulatory liability resulting from the implementation of the Federal Tax Cut and Jobs Act of 2017.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span>
          <br/>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%">We use RSGM for the amortization of (excess)/deficient deferred income taxes to customers. The deferred taxes associated with public utility plant property will be amortized over a period ranging from 3 to 71 years and deferred taxes not related to public utility property will be amortized over a period of 51 years.</span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span>
          <br/>
        </span>
      </div>
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%">The total net (excess)/deficient deferred income tax amortization of $(4,824,761), discussed further in the note shown on page 278 line 2, is reported as the input to page 3, line 24a in our formula rate tariff.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-23" id="fn-23" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%">Pursuant to note AB in our formula rate tariff, our revenue requirement includes the amortization of any net (excess)/deficient deferred income taxes resulting from changes to income tax laws, income tax rates (including changes in apportionment) and other actions taken by a taxing authority.
          <br/>
          <br/>We have a net excess deferred income tax regulatory liability as a result of the annual change in state apportionment factors. We amortize (excess)/deficient deferred income taxes related to apportionment shifts over a one-year period. The amortization of the net (excess)/deficient deferred income taxes is $(233,819). We also have a net (excess)/deficient deferred income tax regulatory liability resulting from the implementation of the Federal Tax Cut and Jobs Act of 2017 as well as the 2018 and 2022 Iowa tax law changes. The amortization of the Federal Tax Cut and Jobs Act of 2017 net (excess)/deficient deferred income taxes is $(3,612,418). The amortization of the Iowa (excess)/deficient deferred income taxes is $(978,524).
          <br/>
          <br/>The total net (excess)/deficient deferred income tax amortization of $(4,824,761) is reported as the input to page 3, line 24a in our formula rate tariff.
        </span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-24" id="fn-24" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:115%">Non-safety related advertising costs of $47,606 are used in our formula rate tariff when reference is to non-safety related advertising in account 930.1 for the current year.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-25" id="fn-25" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="text-align:justify">
