    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-32" id="fn-32" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">ITC Midwest LLC operates within the states of Iowa, Illinois, Minnesota and Wisconsin and utilizes a single aggregate tax rate for tax accounting. The tax rate is calculated using the respective statutory tax rate and apportionment factor formula for each state.&#160;</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-33" id="fn-33" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">ITC Midwest LLC has filings within the states of Iowa, Michigan, and Minnesota.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-34" id="fn-34" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Other taxes primarily includes Sales and Use tax, Federal Highway Use tax, and other taxes and also includes certain activity related to 2024.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-35" id="fn-35" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">ITC Midwest LLC has property tax within the states of Iowa, Illinois, Michigan, Minnesota and Missouri.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-36" id="fn-36" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The activity also reflects prior year adjustments to actual, and certain tax year 2024 payments.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-37" id="fn-37" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Payroll taxes are paid by ITC Holdings Corp. to the various governmental agencies and allocated to its subsidiaries including ITC Midwest LLC.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-38" id="fn-38" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Federal income taxes also reflects certain tax year 2024 activity.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-39" id="fn-39" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">State income taxes also reflects certain tax year 2024 activity.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-40" id="fn-40" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Total other tax is used when reference is to page 263, column l within page 3, line 18, column 3 of our formula rate tariff.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-41" id="fn-41" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Total property tax is used when reference is to page 263, column l within page 3, line 16, column 3 of our formula rate tariff.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-42" id="fn-42" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Total payroll tax is used when reference is to page 263, column l within page 3, line 13, column 3 of our formula rate tariff.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-43" id="fn-43" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">All studies included on this page are generator interconnection studies.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-44" id="fn-44" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The 'Other Accounts' balance represents preliminary charges in account 183 for future capital projects, charges for certain political and related activities in account 426.4 and certain warehouse related labor expenses in account 163.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-45" id="fn-45" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">This includes amounts recorded on a modified Massachusetts Formula allocation policy as described in page 123 Note 4 under "-Cost Assignment" and page 123 Note 10 Related-Party Transactions.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-46" id="fn-46" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">This includes amounts recorded on a modified Massachusetts Formula allocation policy as described in page 123 Note 4 under "-Cost Assignment" and page 123 Note 10 Related-Party Transactions.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-47" id="fn-47" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">This includes amounts recorded on a modified Massachusetts Formula allocation policy as described in page 123 Note 4 under "-Cost Assignment" and page 123 Note 10 Related-Party Transactions.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-48" id="fn-48" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Rental amounts are assigned to ITC Affiliates based on a standardized methodology which identifies, records, and assigns costs related to shared assets and leased facilities to the affiliated business units benefiting from the usage of those shared assets. This standard methodology is generally considered an extension of ITC&#8217;s Direct Assignment Policy.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-49" id="fn-49" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Rental Amounts are assigned to ITC Affiliates based on a standardized methodology which identifies, records, and assigns costs related to shared assets and leased facilities to the affiliated business units benefiting from the usage of those shared assets. This standard methodology is generally considered an extension of ITC's Direct Assignment Policy.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-50" id="fn-50" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The amount represents balances previously recorded to account 397 prior to implementation of FERC Order 898.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-51" id="fn-51" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">This amount represents capitalized depreciation for vehicles and equipment used in the construction process.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-52" id="fn-52" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Net accumulated depreciation related to reserve adjustments persuant to a Commission approved depreciation study on docket #ER-22-3-000, December 3, 2021</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-53" id="fn-53" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The amount of retirements shown differs from the amount of retirements shown on page 204 column (d) due to the retirement of leasehold improvements which are recorded in account 111.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-54" id="fn-54" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The depreciation rates shown in column (e) are straight line rates which when applied to monthly plant balances, will uniformly recover the unrecovered cost, adjusted for net salvage, over the remaining life of the plant.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-55" id="fn-55" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The Average Remaining Life shown in column (g) is based on the latest approved depreciation study, which is based on balances as of December 31, 2020.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-56" id="fn-56" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">In addition to depreciation provided by application of reported rates, the 2025 provision for depreciation was reduced in the amount of $1,081,116 for certain general plant accounts, persuant to implementing the results of the 2021 depreciation study approved by the Commission on December 3, 2021, in docket #ER22-3-000</link:footnote>
