    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-75" id="fn-75" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The transformer at Creston DOE is jointly owned with Central Iowa Power Cooperative, which is not an associated company. See Footnote 9, Jointly Owned Utility Plant / Coordinated Services on page 123.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-76" id="fn-76" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The transformer at Raun is jointly owned with MidAmerica Energy, which is not an associated company. See Footnote 9, Jointly Owned Utility Plant / Coordinated Services on page 123.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-77" id="fn-77" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">All schedules use MISO as billing agent.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-78" id="fn-78" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Network load is populated on Schedule 9 on page 400. No information is provided in column (h) for billing demand, since these pages report Transmission Revenue dollars by schedule and demand information is not readily available (other than Schedule 9) and is maintained by MISO.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-79" id="fn-79" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">ITC Midwest LLC does not report &#8220;Number of Units&#8221; in columns (b), (c),(e) and (f): rather it only reports the total dollars. The quantity is not readily available and information pertaining to the amounts sold and purchased are maintained by MISO.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-80" id="fn-80" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">No information is reported in columns (e) &#8211; (j) as such information is maintained by MISO as the billing agent and not readily available. However, network load is reported in column (b).</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-81" id="fn-81" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">ITC Midwest LLC is a transmission only company and as such, Monthly Energy and Sales for Resale information is not applicable.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-82" id="fn-82" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The First Mortgage Bonds listed were issued under our first mortgage and deed of trust and secured by a first mortgage lien on substantially all of our property.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-83" id="fn-83" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">The debt was issued in 2021 pursuant to Minnesota Statute (2021), Chapter 216E, Section 216E.12 Subd. 3. Repayments for the year ended December 31, 2025 were $290,113.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-84" id="fn-84" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">On January 31, 2024, the commission issued an order in Docket No. ES24-19-000 authorizing us to issue senior secured notes or other long-term debt up to $300 million, expiring on January 30, 2026. We have $50 million of authorization remaining as of December 31, 2025.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-85" id="fn-85" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">During the year ended December 31, 2025, we borrowed $498,600,000 and repaid $371,400,000 under the revolving credit agreement.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-86" id="fn-86" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents borrowings under the revolving credit agreement.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-87" id="fn-87" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents issuance of long-term debt of $250,000,000 and borrowings under the revolving credit agreement of $419,400,000.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-88" id="fn-88" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents repayments of the revolving credit agreement of $371,400,000 and repayments of the Hiniker Installment Purchase of $290,113.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-89" id="fn-89" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents repayments of long-term debt of $75,000,000, repayments of the revolving credit agreement of $518,400,000 and repayments of the Hiniker Installment Purchase of $290,113.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-90" id="fn-90" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents cash balance in accounts 131 and 136.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-91" id="fn-91" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Represents cash balance in accounts 131 and 136.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-92" id="fn-92" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">In compliance with Schedule 50 Order approved on March 19, 2020 under the Federal Regulatory Commission docket number ER20-170, ITC Midwest invoices the generators for annual operations and maintenance costs associated with Transmission Owner&#8217;s Interconnection Facilities calculated for actual year 2024, pursuant to Article 10, Section 10.5 of their Generator Interconnection Agreement.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-93" id="fn-93" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Amounts shown as transfers in column (f) from account 391 were solely for the purpose of implementing FERC Order 898 and represent transfers of computer hardware, software and communication equipment to newly established plant accounts 351.1, 351.2, 351.3, 397.1, 397.2, 397.3.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-94" id="fn-94" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Other minor timing differences associated with operating income and expenses.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-95" id="fn-95" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Other minor timing differences associated with below the line operating income and expenses.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-96" id="fn-96" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">A portion of the deferred amounts are amortized over a term that ends October 27, 2035.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-97" id="fn-97" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Other minor timing differences associated with below the line operating income and expenses.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-98" id="fn-98" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Other minor non-plant timing differences primarily associated with tax gross-up on state deficient deferred income tax regulatory asset.</link:footnote>
